Test rg75: a slash then a comment
// A slash with no blank before it, then a // comment, at the end of a bare
// statement's first expression is an origin, and the comment follows it.
// In "200// c" the two slashes are the comment, so it is the word 200, and a
// slash then a comment in a statement that is not bare stays a word too.
100/
    cla                 // 0100
    hlt// c             // 0101: hlt, then the comment
    200// c             // 0102: the word 200
    300//* c */         // 0103: the word 300, a /* in mid line is not a comment
x,  4/// c              // 0104: the word 4, the label ends the bare statement
120/// an origin, then this comment
    lac x               // 0120: lac 0104
130+10/// the origin is an expression: 0140
    lac 1               // 0140
    cla; 150/// cla at 0141, then the origin after the ';'
    nop                 // 0150
160/
y,
170/
    0                   // 0170
y/// the origin is a label: 0160
    lac y               // 0160: lac 0160
start 100
